  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 245 PM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nMonday, as the trough continues ejecting intl the upper Midwest, the \ntail end of it moves through West texas and Southeast New Mexico, \nyielding the coldest day this forecast as highs struggle to come in \n~ 3-4 F below normal, leaving most locations in the upper 60s and \nlower 70s.  As the trough moves through, Monday afternoon looks to \nbe the best chance at rain this forecast.\n\nTuesday/Wednesday, temperatures will rebound 5-10 degrees or so as a \ndry southwest flow aloft develops over the region.  An upper trough \nwill begin strengthening over the PacNW, then digging down the west \ncoast as the week progresses.  Rain chances begin ramping up again \nbeginning Thursday as shortwave disturbances move through southwest \nflow aloft, peaking Friday night as a weak Pac front moves\nthrough.",
